  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Q: How does the Client & Frontend interface with DataForge?",
      "items": [
        "A: Users access the React 18 SPA (Vite + TypeScript) on port 3000 delivering 16 views for profiling, schema editing, and ML readiness.",
        "A: The frontend uses Axios API client with Bearer JWT tokens to execute synchronous REST operations over /api/v1."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Q: How are API requests, authentication, and core routes handled?",
      "items": [
        "A: FastAPI on port 8000 executes asynchronous Python routes for datasets, schemas, version diffs, and ML scoring.",
        "A: PyJWT & Passlib handle authentication, while SQLAlchemy 2.0 ORM persists relational metadata in PostgreSQL 16 (port 5432)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Q: How does Asynchronous Background Execution operate for heavy dataset workloads?",
      "items": [
        "A: FastAPI pushes long-running tasks (data profiling, transformation DAGs, ML scoring) to Redis 7 message broker (port 6379).",
        "A: Celery background workers dequeue tasks and execute compute workloads without blocking HTTP response threads."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Q: How are compute profiling and dataset transformation engines structured?",
      "items": [
        "A: The Data Engine leverages Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-Learn, and SciPy to calculate skewness, missingness, correlation matrices, and ML readiness scores.",
        "A: Processed datasets are serialized to optimized Apache Parquet and CSV formats using PyArrow."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Q: How is persistence, object storage, and version lineage managed?",
      "items": [
        "A: PostgreSQL storing user accounts, dataset schemas, transformation pipelines, and git-like version lineage trees.",
        "A: MinIO S3 object storage (ports 9000/9001) persists raw uploads and transformed dataset versions in dataforge-datasets buckets."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
